# Build artifacts, not source.
#
# `/starpoint` at the repo root is `go build`'s default-named binary, and
# `/bin/` and `/dist/` are the Makefile's and goreleaser's outputs. None is
# source; the scanner reports binaries as skipped rather than scanned, so
# without these entries every run pays one INFO note for zero coverage. The
# history scan already shows the cost of that: the binary was committed once,
# and every blob of it is just a binary-skip note. The patterns are anchored to
# the repo root so `cmd/starpoint/` is never caught by the binary's name.
#
# Test files are skipped by minesweep's own default (`--include-tests` includes
# them). That default was measured too: with tests included, the suite scans
# clean at the config's 0.7 floor. This file deliberately adds nothing on top.
#
# The scanner's own config is settings, not secrets.
.minesweep.yml

/starpoint
/bin/
/dist/
